{
  "info": {
    "name": "FixNow Admin Runtime",
    "description": "End-to-end Admin runtime (Sprint 6.7).\n\nConsolidates every admin endpoint shipped in Sprints 5.1.4 + 6.0 → 6.6 into one runnable narrative:\n  01 Auth — admin login (mobile mode, captures adminToken)\n  02 User Control (Sprint 6.1) — list / search / detail / PATCH status / roles\n  03 Provider Verification (Sprint 6.2) — list / detail / audit / review-notes / approve/reject/suspend/reactivate\n  04 Disputes (Sprint 6.3) — list / filter / detail / PATCH / resolve\n  05 Analytics (Sprint 6.4) — overview / revenue\n  06 Financials (Sprint 6.4) — summary / bookings / provider-earnings\n  07 Settings (Sprint 6.5) — bulk GET / valid PATCH / invalid PATCH\n  08 Admin Notifications (Sprint 6.6) — list / mark read\n  09 Audit Logs (Sprint 6.6) — list / filter by action / redaction check\n  10 Negative Security — customer-token 403 + no-token 401 + IDOR-style query rejection\n\nBefore running:\n  - Boot the API at http://localhost:4000.\n  - Pre-seed an admin account (one-time): see docs/testing/provider-runtime-loop.md §2 for the Prisma snippet that grants the admin role.\n  - Pre-seed a customer (non-admin) account so folder 10's negatives can fire.\n  - Copy postman/local.postman_environment.example.json → postman/local.postman_environment.json and fill in the email/password fields for both accounts.\n  - Run folder 01 first: it captures adminToken and customerToken into the environment.\n\nEvery request runs the collection-level Prisma/SQL/secret-leak guard.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "fixnow-admin-runtime"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "apiUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000" },
    { "key": "apiVersion", "value": "v1" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const text = pm.response.text();",
          "pm.test('no Prisma/SQL/secret leak', () => {",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.match(/PrismaClient|column .* does not exist|SELECT |INSERT |UPDATE /i);",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('passwordHash');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('mfaSecret');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('refreshToken');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('JWT_SECRET');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('DATABASE_URL');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('STRIPE_SECRET');",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 — Auth",
      "description": "Admin + customer login. Captures bearer tokens into env vars used by every later folder.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/auth/login (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.tokens && body.tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('adminToken', body.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.test('captured adminToken', () => pm.expect(body.tokens.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else if (body.otpRequired) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('adminOtpChallengeId', body.challengeId);",
                  "  pm.test('OTP challenge captured', () => pm.expect(body.challengeId).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test.fail('login response carried neither tokens nor OTP challenge');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/auth/login (customer — for negatives)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.tokens && body.tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('customerToken', body.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/auth/me (admin role check)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/auth/me"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const me = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"roles[] contains 'admin'\", () => pm.expect(me.roles).to.include('admin'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('adminUserId', me.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 — User Control (Sprint 6.1)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/admin/users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/admin/users?limit=10"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('cursor pagination shape', () => pm.expect(body).to.have.property('nextCursor'));",
                  "pm.test('no passwordHash/mfaSecret on the wire', () => {",
                  "  const t = pm.response.text();",
                  "  pm.expect(t).to.not.include('passwordHash');",
                  "  pm.expect(t).to.not.include('mfaSecret');",
                  "});",
                  "if (body.items.length > 0) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('targetUserId', body.items.find(u => !u.roles.includes('admin'))?.id ?? body.items[0].id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/admin/users?query=test (search)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/admin/users?query=test&limit=5"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().items).to.be.an('array'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/admin/users/:id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/admin/users/{{targetUserId}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 or 404', () => pm.expect([200, 404]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PATCH /v1/admin/users/:id/status (suspend → restore round-trip)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/admin/users/{{targetUserId}}/status",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"reason\": \"runtime — restore to known state\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 / 400 (self-disable refused) / 404', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect([200, 400, 404]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.test('user.status echoes the patch', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().user.status).to.eql('ACTIVE'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/admin/roles",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/admin/roles"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"seeded 'admin' role present\", () => pm.expect(body.items.some(r => r.name === 'admin')).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
